{
  "id": "ep169",
  "duration": 47.684,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 3.901,
      "text": "A human sprint could launch you straight into orbit around Mars.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "NASA-Deimos-MarsMoon-20090221.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL/University of Arizona",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NASA-Deimos-MarsMoon-20090221.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 3.9,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 3.901,
      "end": 10.445,
      "text": "In August 1877, astronomer Asaph Hall was ready to give up his search for Martian moons.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Professor Asaph Hall.jpg",
        "credit": "Unknown author",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Professor_Asaph_Hall.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 3.9,
          "end": 10.433,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 10.445,
      "end": 16.816,
      "text": "His wife, Angeline Stickney, urged him to continue his search at the US Naval Observatory.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Angeline Stickney.jpg",
        "credit": "Unknown authorUnknown author",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Angeline_Stickney.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 10.433,
          "end": 16.8,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 16.816,
      "end": 23.96,
      "text": "Hall discovered Deimos, a smooth, dusty moon twelve kilometers wide that acts like a cosmic springboard.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Deimos viking2.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Deimos_viking2.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 16.8,
          "end": 23.967,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 23.96,
      "end": 30.285,
      "text": "Its surface gravity is so weak that its escape velocity is only 13 miles per hour.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "NASA Mars Rover.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL/Cornell University, Maas Digital LLC",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NASA_Mars_Rover.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 23.967,
          "end": 28.1,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 28.1,
          "end": 30.3,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 30.285,
      "end": 36.93,
      "text": "That is slower than a fast human runner, meaning a simple sprint overcomes the moon\u2019s entire gravity.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "NASA Mars Rover.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL/Cornell University, Maas Digital LLC",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NASA_Mars_Rover.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 30.3,
          "end": 36.933,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 36.93,
      "end": 43.325,
      "text": "While its sister moon Phobos is spiraling toward Mars, Deimos is slowly drifting away into space.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Phobos and Mars - ESA Mars Express (52537343727).png",
        "credit": "Andrea Luck",
        "license": "CC BY 2.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Phobos_and_Mars_-_ESA_Mars_Express_(52537343727).png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 36.933,
          "end": 40.133,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 40.133,
          "end": 43.333,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 43.325,
      "end": 47.334,
      "text": "On Deimos, a simple sprint is enough to reach escape velocity.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "NASA-Deimos-MarsMoon-20090221.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL/University of Arizona",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NASA-Deimos-MarsMoon-20090221.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 43.333,
          "end": 47.7,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
